{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAkN56GKQP4kMDdDCu4RpY","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 79314f3cae59b6f24693622ff06c296c515bd1bf\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Mon Apr 13 02:16:55 2026 +0200\n\n    Batch stacking scatter kernel: replace per-column CUDA calls with single kernel\n    \n    Replace ~106K individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync + batch_expand_pad_wide\n    kernel launches) in stack_traces_into_expanded() with a two-phase approach:\n    \n    1. Build a descriptor array on the CPU (no CUDA overhead per column)\n    2. Upload descriptors to GPU and launch a single scatter kernel\n    \n    Each CUDA block handles one column descriptor, with threads cooperatively copying\n    elements from source to destination with configurable stride.\n    \n    At APC 300: Trace Commit improved 1.62x (414ms -> 255ms), D2D memcpy count\n    dropped from 101K to 325. No regression at APC 0.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/matrix.rs | 26 ++++++++++++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs       |  8 +++---\n crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs | 48 ++++++++++++++--------------------\n 4 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D4gDZrAY1XdvhKesTMUn8g","session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"7a404b5b-7b5d-46bc-aeca-950ab797846f","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:09:40.477Z"}
