*: `(num_blocks, num_x)` — 2D grid\n  - `num_blocks = sum over AIRs of (ceil(num_monomials / tpb) * num_y)`\n  - `num_x = sp_deg` (constraint degree), e.g., 2 or 3\n- **Block**: `(threads_per_block,)` — typically 256\n- **Shared memory**: `ceil(threads_per_block / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)` bytes for block reduction\n\n#### Block Assignment Logic (lines 117-120):\n```cuda\nuint32_t mono_blocks = (num_monomials + threads_per_block - 1) / threads_per_block;\nuint32_t y_int = local_block_idx_x / mono_blocks;\nuint32_t mono_block = local_block_idx_x % mono_blocks;\n```\n- Each block handles one (y_int, mono_block) pair\n- Thread m evaluates monomial `m = mono_block * threads_per_block + threadIdx.x`\n- Variable evaluation: `row = x_int * num_y + y_int`\n\n#### Kernel Implementation:\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu` lines 102-151\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_monomial_kernel(\n    FpExt *tmp_sums,\n    const BlockCtx *block_ctxs,\n    const MonomialAirCtx *air_ctxs,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n) {\n    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n    FpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n    \n    BlockCtx bctx = block_ctxs[blockIdx.x];\n    MonomialAirCtx actx = air_ctxs[bctx.air_idx];\n    \n    uint32_t num_x = gridDim.y;\n    uint32_t x_int = blockIdx.y;\n    \n    uint32_t mono_blocks = (actx.num_monomials + threads_per_block - 1) / threads_per_block;\n    uint32_t y_int = bctx.local_block_idx_x / mono_blocks;\n    uint32_t mono_block = bctx.local_block_idx_x % mono_blocks;\n    \n    uint32_t height = num_x * actx.num_y;\n    uint32_t row = x_int * actx.num_y + y_int;\n    \n    FpExt sum(Fp::zero());\n    uint32_t m = mono_block * threads_per_block + threadIdx.x;\n    if (m < actx.num_monomials) {\n        MonomialHeader hdr = actx.d_headers[m];\n        FpExt product(Fp::one());\n        for (uint16_t v = 0; v < hdr.num_vars; ++v) {\n            PackedVar var = actx.d_variables[hdr.var_offset + v];\n            product *= eval_variable(var, row, actx.eval_ctx, height);\n        }\n        sum = product * actx.d_lambda_combinations[m];\n    }\n    \n    FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(sum, shared);\n    if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n        reduced *= actx.d_eq_xi[y_int];\n        tmp_sums[blockIdx.x * num_x + x_int] = reduced;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Per-Trace vs Shared Data:\n| Data | Per-Trace | Shared |\n|------|-----------|--------|\n| `block_ctxs` | Global array | (all traces batched) |\n| `air_ctxs` | One per AIR, organized in array | - |\n| `d_headers` | YES (per-AIR) | - |\n| `d_variables` | YES (per-AIR) | - |\n| `d_lambda_combinations` | YES (per-AIR, from precompute) | - |\n| `d_selectors` | YES (per-trace) | - |\n| `d_preprocessed`, `d_main` | YES (per-trace) | - |\n| `d_eq_xi` | YES (per-trace, length num_y) | - |\n\n**D2H Sync Points**: \n- Line 1849 in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`: `out.to_host()?`\n\n---\n\n### 3. **zerocheck_monomial_par_y_kernel** (18ms, 43 instances ~418us each)\n\n#### What it computes:\nParallelizes over y_int instead of monomials. Each thread handles one y_int and loops over a chunk of monomials:\n```\nper_thread: sum_over_monomials[chunk]: product_of_variables[m] * d_lambda_combinations[m]\nApply: result *= d_eq_xi[y_int]\nBlock-reduce across y_int values\n```\n\n#### Data Layout (same as zerocheck_monomial_kernel, with additional parameter):\n| Parameter | Type | Size | Description |\n|-----------|------|------|-------------|\n| `chunk_size` | `u32` | 1 | Monomials per chunk (auto-tuned) |\n\n**Additional encoding in local_block_idx_x:**\n```\nEncoding: local_block_idx_x = y_block * air_mono_chunks + mono_chunk\nwhere:\n  y_block = local_block_idx_x / air_mono_chunks\n  mono_chunk = local_block_idx_x % air_mono_chunks\n  air_mono_chunks = ceil(num_monomials / chunk_size)\n```\n\n#### Grid/Block Configuration:\n- **Grid**: `(num_blocks, num_x)`\n- **Block**: `(threads_per_block,)` — typically 128 (vs 256 for monomial_kernel)\n- **Shared memory**: `ceil(threads_per_block / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)`\n\n#### Chunk Size Auto-tuning (batch_mle_monomial.rs lines 342-368):\n```rust\nconst THREADS_PER_BLOCK_PAR_Y: u32 = 128;\nconst DEFAULT_MAX_MONOMIALS_PER_THREAD: u32 = 64;\nconst WAVES_TARGET: u32 = 4;\n\n// Ensure: total_blocks * num_x >= sm_count * WAVES_TARGET\nlet target_blocks = sm_count * WAVES_TARGET;\nlet mut chunk_size = max_mono_per_thread;\nloop {\n    let total_blocks: u32 = per_air_info.iter()\n        .map(|(y_blocks, num_mono)| {\n            let air_mono_chunks = num_mono.div_ceil(chunk_size);\n            y_blocks * air_mono_chunks\n        })\n        .sum();\n    \n    if total_blocks * num_x >= target_blocks || chunk_size <= 1 {\n        break;\n    }\n    chunk_size = (chunk_size / 2).max(1);\n}\n```\n\n#### Kernel Implementation:\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu` lines 198-256\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_monomial_par_y_kernel(\n    FpExt *tmp_sums,\n    const BlockCtx *block_ctxs,\n    const MonomialAirCtx *air_ctxs,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block,\n    uint32_t chunk_size\n) {\n    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n    FpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n    \n    BlockCtx bctx = block_ctxs[blockIdx.x];\n    MonomialAirCtx actx = air_ctxs[bctx.air_idx];\n    \n    uint32_t num_x = gridDim.y;\n    uint32_t x_int = blockIdx.y;\n    \n    uint32_t air_mono_chunks = (actx.num_monomials + chunk_size - 1) / chunk_size;\n    uint32_t y_block = bctx.local_block_idx_x / air_mono_chunks;\n    uint32_t mono_chunk = bctx.local_block_idx_x % air_mono_chunks;\n    \n    uint32_t y_int = threadIdx.x + y_block * threads_per_block;\n    bool active = (y_int < actx.num_y);\n    \n    uint32_t height = num_x * actx.num_y;\n    uint32_t row = x_int * actx.num_y + y_int;\n    \n    uint32_t mono_start = mono_chunk * chunk_size;\n    uint32_t mono_end = min(mono_start + chunk_size, actx.num_monomials);\n    \n    FpExt sum(Fp::zero());\n    if (active) {\n        for (uint32_t m = mono_start; m < mono_end; ++m) {\n            MonomialHeader hdr = actx.d_headers[m];\n            FpExt product(Fp::one());\n            for (uint16_t v = 0; v < hdr.num_vars; ++v) {\n                PackedVar var = actx.d_variables[hdr.var_offset + v];\n                product *= eval_variable(var, row, actx.eval_ctx, height);\n            }\n            sum += product * actx.d_lambda_combinations[m];\n        }\n        sum *= actx.d_eq_xi[y_int];\n    }\n    \n    FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(sum, shared);\n    if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n        tmp_sums[blockIdx.x * num_x + x_int] = reduced;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Per-Trace vs Shared Data: Same as zerocheck_monomial_kernel\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Batched Reduction (sumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums)**\n\n#### What it does:\nReduces per-block sums across all blocks for each AIR in a single batched launch.\n\n**File**: Not fully visible in search, but called from:\n- `_zerocheck_monomial_batched()` line 187 in batch_mle_monomial.cu\n- `_zerocheck_monomial_par_y_batched()` line 292 in batch_mle_monomial.cu\n\n#### Launch:\n```cuda\ndim3 reduce_grid(num_airs, num_x);\nsumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums<<<reduce_grid, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    tmp_sums, output, air_block_offsets, num_x\n);\n```\n- **Grid**: `(num_airs, num_x)` — one block per (air, x) pair\n- **Block size**: Auto-computed from `kernel_launch_params(num_blocks / num_airs + 1)`\n- **Inputs**: `tmp_sums[num_blocks * num_x]`, `air_block_offsets[num_airs + 1]`\n- **Output**: `output[num_airs * num_x]`\n\n**air_block_offsets layout**: \n- `air_block_offsets[i]` = start index in tmp_sums for AIR i\n- `air_block_offsets[num_airs]` = total num_blocks\n- Allows reduction to sum blocks `[air_block_offsets[i], air_block_offsets[i+1])` per AIR\n\n---\n\n## 5. **Orchestration Call Chain (Rust)**\n\n### Ent