array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains.","+Overlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37ms GPU time) plus ~791 H2D uploads (~5-8ms) run sequentially on the default stream BEFORE Round 0 starts, even though their output is only consumed later during MLE rounds. Round 0 uses only host-side eq_3b values for weight computation, so the device-side precompute is entirely independent. By spawning the precompute on a background thread concurrent with Round 0 (which runs 155ms on 8 streams at ~42% GPU utilization), the ~45ms of precompute work is hidden behind the longer Round 0 phase."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction\n\nMove the per-AIR polynomial extraction in Round 0 (D2H sync + transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment) from CPU to a small CUDA kernel that runs on the same stream immediately after each evaluation kernel. This eliminates all per-AIR `cudaStreamSynchronize` calls in the multi-stream Round 0 loop and the ~40ms of CPU post-processing per thread, replacing them with a negligible GPU-side computation that writes polynomial coefficients directly into a device-side batch array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains.\n"}}
