{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0132s9CCw5UJev2chwSGe2tG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011m5PSakDxi9ReRkMkmPJiA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Overlap Logup Combination Precompute with Round 0\n\n## Goal\n\nHide ~45ms of logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b H2D uploads + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) behind the ~155ms Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running them concurrently on a background thread. This removes the precompute from Round 0's critical path, reducing STARK excl trace by ~35-45ms at APC 300 without regressing APC 0.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n**Function**: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (line 882)\n\nCurrent sequential order within this function:\n\n1. **Lines 893-908**: Lambda powers upload + lambda combination precompute (needed for Round 0)\n2. **Lines 912-944**: eq_3b host-side CPU computation (needed for Round 0 weight computation — each work item borrows `&self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx]` at line 1082)\n3. **Lines 945-955**: d_eq_3b device upload — 791 `to_device()` calls producing `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace`. NOT needed for Round 0. Only used by step 4.\n4. **Lines 957-975**: logup_combinations precompute — iterates over all traces, calls `compute_logup_combinations()` per trace. Each call launches 2 GPU kernels (`precompute_logup_numer_combinations` + `precompute_logup_denom_combinations`). 1582 total kernel launches, 37ms GPU time. NOT needed for Round 0, only for MLE rounds.\n5. **Lines 977-1002**: eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base (needed for Round 0 work items)\n6. **Lines 1014-1137**: Work item construction, sorting, extract tables, batch array\n7. **Line 1192-1194**: `current_stream_sync()` barrier\n8. **Lines 1196+**: Round 0 multi-stream evaluation (~155ms, 8 threads)\n\nSteps 3-4 total ~45ms and are independent of steps 5-8. Round 0 GPU utilization is ~42%, leaving ample capacity for concurrent precompute kernels.\n\n**Data dependency analysis:**\n\n| Data | Used by Round 0? | Used by precompute? | Conflict? |\n|------|-------------------|---------------------|-----------|\n| `self.pk` | Yes (shared &) | Yes (shared &) | No (both read-only) |\n| `self.eq_3b_per_trace` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]`) | Yes (read for upload + CPU bus_term_sum) | No (both read-only) |\n| `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace` (device) | No | Yes (written by upload) | No conflict |\n| `self.d_beta_pows` | No (Round 0 uses host-side `beta_pows`) | Yes (read by precompute kernels) | No |\n| `self.logup_combinations` | No | Yes (written by precompute) | No conflict |\n| `self.beta_pows` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]`) | Yes (read for bus_term_sum CPU computation) | No (both read-only) |\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Restructure `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` to overlap precompute with Round 0\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n**What**: Reorder the function body so that steps 3-4 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) run on a background thread concurrent with step 8 (Round 0 multi-stream evaluation).\n\n**New flow**:\n\n```\n1. Lambda powers + lambda combinations            (sequential, same as before)\n2. eq_3b CPU computation → self.eq_3b_per_trace    (sequential, same as before)\n3. eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base                    (sequential, MOVED BEFORE precompute)\n4. Work item construction + sorting + extract tables + batch array  (sequential)\n5. current_stream_sync() barrier\n6. std::thread::scope:\n   ├─ Background thread: d_eq_3b upload + logup_combinations precompute\n   │   → returns (Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>>, Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>>)\n   │   → calls current_stream_sync() before returning (ensures GPU work visible)\n   └─ Round 0 worker threads (0..num_threads): process_air_round0 (same as before)\n7. Store background thread results: self.d_eq_3b_per_trace, self.logup_combinations\n```\n\n**Specific code changes**:\n\na) **Move lines 945-975 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) out of their current position** into a closure that runs inside the `thread::scope` block.\n\nb) **Move lines 977-1002 (eq_xis + sels) to before the removed lines** — they currently sit between the precompute and work item construction but are independent. Moving them earlier doesn't change behavior.\n\nc) **Inside the existing `thread::scope` block** (which currently only spawns Round 0 worker threads), spawn one additional background thread:\n\n```rust\nlet precompute_handle = s.spawn(|| {\n    // Upload d_eq_3b to device (same code as lines 945-955)\n    let d_eq_3b: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = eq_3b_per_trace_ref\n        .iter()\n        .map(|eq_3bs| {\n            if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n                Ok(DeviceBuffer::new())\n            } else {\n                eq_3bs.to_device()\n            }\n        })\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n\n    // Precompute logup combinations (same code as lines 957-975)\n    let mut logup_combs: Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>> =\n        (0..num_present_airs).map(|_| None).collect();\n    for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in per_trace_ref.iter().enumerate() {\n        let air_pk = &pk_ref.per_air[*air_idx];\n        if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some()\n            && !eq_3b_per_trace_ref[trace_idx].is_empty()\n        {\n            logup_combs[trace_idx] = Some(compute_logup_combinations(\n                pk_ref,\n                *air_idx,\n                d_beta_pows_ref,\n                &d_eq_3b[trace_idx],\n                &eq_3b_per_trace_ref[trace_idx],\n                beta_pows_ref,\n            )?);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Ensure all GPU work on this thread's stream is complete\n    current_stream_sync()?;\n\n    Ok((d_eq_3b, logup_combs))\n});\n```\n\nd) **After all threads join** (after the `thread::scope` block), store the background results:\n\n```rust\nlet (d_eq_3b, logup_combs) = precompute_result?;\nself.d_eq_3b_per_trace = d_eq_3b;\nself.logup_combinations = logup_combs;\n```\n\ne) **Remove the original lines 945-975** (now handled by the background thread).\n\n### Change 2: Handle borrow references for the background thread\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nThe background thread closure needs shared references to:\n- `self.pk` (via a local reference like `let pk_ref = self.pk;`)\n- `self.eq_3b_per_trace` (via a local reference)\n- `self.d_beta_pows` (via a local reference)\n- `self.beta_pows` (via a local reference)\n- `ctx.per_trace` (via a local reference)\n\nThese are all shared borrows (`&`) that can coexist with the shared borrows taken by Round 0 work items. Use `let pk = self.pk; let eq_3b = &self.eq_3b_per_trace;` etc. before the `thread::scope` block to create reference bindings that the scope can capture.\n\nThe `thread::scope` API ensures all spawned threads complete before the scope exits, so all borrows are valid for the thread's lifetime.\n\n### Change 3: Adjust the `current_stream_sync` barrier position\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nThe existing `current_stream_sync()` at line 1192 ensures prior GPU work is visible to worker threads. Since the background thread does its own GPU uploads and kernel launches on `cudaStreamPerThread`, it has its own implicit stream ordering. The background thread's `current_stream_sync()` at the end ensures its work is complete before the results are used in MLE rounds.\n\nThe existing barrier at line 1192 must remain — it ensures that GPU data uploaded by the main thread (sels, lambda_pows, batch_array, extract tables) is visible to the Round 0 worker threads.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: The logup_combinations values are identical — same inputs, same computation, same results. Only the timing changes.\n2. **Stream safety**: The background thread's `cudaStreamPerThread` is independent from the Round 0 worker threads' `cudaStreamPerThread`s. The background thread calls `current_stream_sync()` before returning, ensuring all its GPU work (H2D copies, kernel launches, memory allocations) is complete and visible to all streams.\n3. **No APC 0 regression**: At APC 0, `num_threads = 1` (< 100 AIRs). The background precompute thread still spawns but does minimal work (~5ms for ~99 traces). The single-threaded Round 0 is unaffected.\n4. **Memory pool safety**: The background thread allocates DeviceBuffers through `cudaMallocAsync` on its own stream. These are small allocations (~100 EF elements per trace, total ~600KB). They don't interfere with the Round 0 worker threads' pre-allocated buffers.\n5. **Borrow safety**: All references captured by the background thread are shared borrows (`&`) that coexist with the shared borrows held by Round 0 work items. No mutable aliases exist during the `thread::scope` lifetime.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nRun the benchmark in `/home/georg/powdr`:\n```bash\ncd results/pairing\nRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\nRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n```\n\nAnalyze with `spec.py`:\n```bash\npython3 ~/spec.py current_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\npython3 ~/spec.py current_apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\n```\n\nExpected results:\n- Round 0 at APC 300: 202ms → ~160ms (20% reduction)\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1327ms → ~1285ms\n- APC 0: no regression (within ±10ms noise)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if ANY of:\n- Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 25ms (below noise threshold)\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses vs before\n- Any metric at APC 0 regresses by more than 20ms\n- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":410,"cache_read_input_tokens":164781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":410},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"11394fc5-9a45-4989-99c9-4ad3f4d2bc74"}
