{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018LnmDMdgzXqWe3YPmb3Uq4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Overlap Logup Combination Precompute with Round 0\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tHide ~45ms of logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b H2D uploads + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) behind the ~155ms Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running them concurrently on a background thread. This removes the precompute from Round 0's critical path, reducing STARK excl trace by ~35-45ms at APC 300 without regressing APC 0.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n10\t\n11\t**Function**: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (line 882)\n12\t\n13\tCurrent sequential order within this function:\n14\t\n15\t1. **Lines 893-908**: Lambda powers upload + lambda combination precompute (needed for Round 0)\n16\t2. **Lines 912-944**: eq_3b host-side CPU computation (needed for Round 0 weight computation — each work item borrows `&self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx]` at line 1082)\n17\t3. **Lines 945-955**: d_eq_3b device upload — 791 `to_device()` calls producing `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace`. NOT needed for Round 0. Only used by step 4.\n18\t4. **Lines 957-975**: logup_combinations precompute — iterates over all traces, calls `compute_logup_combinations()` per trace. Each call launches 2 GPU kernels (`precompute_logup_numer_combinations` + `precompute_logup_denom_combinations`). 1582 total kernel launches, 37ms GPU time. NOT needed for Round 0, only for MLE rounds.\n19\t5. **Lines 977-1002**: eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base (needed for Round 0 work items)\n20\t6. **Lines 1014-1137**: Work item construction, sorting, extract tables, batch array\n21\t7. **Line 1192-1194**: `current_stream_sync()` barrier\n22\t8. **Lines 1196+**: Round 0 multi-stream evaluation (~155ms, 8 threads)\n23\t\n24\tSteps 3-4 total ~45ms and are independent of steps 5-8. Round 0 GPU utilization is ~42%, leaving ample capacity for concurrent precompute kernels.\n25\t\n26\t**Data dependency analysis:**\n27\t\n28\t| Data | Used by Round 0? | Used by precompute? | Conflict? |\n29\t|------|-------------------|---------------------|-----------|\n30\t| `self.pk` | Yes (shared &) | Yes (shared &) | No (both read-only) |\n31\t| `self.eq_3b_per_trace` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]`) | Yes (read for upload + CPU bus_term_sum) | No (both read-only) |\n32\t| `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace` (device) | No | Yes (written by upload) | No conflict |\n33\t| `self.d_beta_pows` | No (Round 0 uses host-side `beta_pows`) | Yes (read by precompute kernels) | No |\n34\t| `self.logup_combinations` | No | Yes (written by precompute) | No conflict |\n35\t| `self.beta_pows` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]`) | Yes (read for bus_term_sum CPU computation) | No (both read-only) |\n36\t\n37\t## Changes\n38\t\n39\t### Change 1: Restructure `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` to overlap precompute with Round 0\n40\t\n41\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n42\t\n43\t**What**: Reorder the function body so that steps 3-4 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) run on a background thread concurrent with step 8 (Round 0 multi-stream evaluation).\n44\t\n45\t**New flow**:\n46\t\n47\t```\n48\t1. Lambda powers + lambda combinations            (sequential, same as before)\n49\t2. eq_3b CPU computation → self.eq_3b_per_trace    (sequential, same as before)\n50\t3. eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base                    (sequential, MOVED BEFORE precompute)\n51\t4. Work item construction + sorting + extract tables + batch array  (sequential)\n52\t5. current_stream_sync() barrier\n53\t6. std::thread::scope:\n54\t   ├─ Background thread: d_eq_3b upload + logup_combinations precompute\n55\t   │   → returns (Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>>, Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>>)\n56\t   │   → calls current_stream_sync() before returning (ensures GPU work visible)\n57\t   └─ Round 0 worker threads (0..num_threads): process_air_round0 (same as before)\n58\t7. Store background thread results: self.d_eq_3b_per_trace, self.logup_combinations\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\t**Specific code changes**:\n62\t\n63\ta) **Move lines 945-975 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) out of their current position** into a closure that runs inside the `thread::scope` block.\n64\t\n65\tb) **Move lines 977-1002 (eq_xis + sels) to before the removed lines** — they currently sit between the precompute and work item construction but are independent. Moving them earlier doesn't change behavior.\n66\t\n67\tc) **Inside the existing `thread::scope` block** (which currently only spawns Round 0 worker threads), spawn one additional background thread:\n68\t\n69\t```rust\n70\tlet precompute_handle = s.spawn(|| {\n71\t    // Upload d_eq_3b to device (same code as lines 945-955)\n72\t    let d_eq_3b: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = eq_3b_per_trace_ref\n73\t        .iter()\n74\t        .map(|eq_3bs| {\n75\t            if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n76\t                Ok(DeviceBuffer::new())\n77\t            } else {\n78\t                eq_3bs.to_device()\n79\t            }\n80\t        })\n81\t        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n82\t\n83\t    // Precompute logup combinations (same code as lines 957-975)\n84\t    let mut logup_combs: Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>> =\n85\t        (0..num_present_airs).map(|_| None).collect();\n86\t    for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in per_trace_ref.iter().enumerate() {\n87\t        let air_pk = &pk_ref.per_air[*air_idx];\n88\t        if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some()\n89\t            && !eq_3b_per_trace_ref[trace_idx].is_empty()\n90\t        {\n91\t            logup_combs[trace_idx] = Some(compute_logup_combinations(\n92\t                pk_ref,\n93\t                *air_idx,\n94\t                d_beta_pows_ref,\n95\t                &d_eq_3b[trace_idx],\n96\t                &eq_3b_per_trace_ref[trace_idx],\n97\t                beta_pows_ref,\n98\t            )?);\n99\t        }\n100\t    }\n101\t\n102\t    // Ensure all GPU work on this thread's stream is complete\n103\t    current_stream_sync()?;\n104\t\n105\t    Ok((d_eq_3b, logup_combs))\n106\t});\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\td) **After all threads join** (after the `thread::scope` block), store the background results:\n110\t\n111\t```rust\n112\tlet (d_eq_3b, logup_combs) = precompute_result?;\n113\tself.d_eq_3b_per_trace = d_eq_3b;\n114\tself.logup_combinations = logup_combs;\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\te) **Remove the original lines 945-975** (now handled by the background thread).\n118\t\n119\t### Change 2: Handle borrow references for the background thread\n120\t\n121\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n122\t\n123\tThe background thread closure needs shared references to:\n124\t- `self.pk` (via a local reference like `let pk_ref = self.pk;`)\n125\t- `self.eq_3b_per_trace` (via a local reference)\n126\t- `self.d_beta_pows` (via a local reference)\n127\t- `self.beta_pows` (via a local reference)\n128\t- `ctx.per_trace` (via a local reference)\n129\t\n130\tThese are all shared borrows (`&`) that can coexist with the shared borrows taken by Round 0 work items. Use `let pk = self.pk; let eq_3b = &self.eq_3b_per_trace;` etc. before the `thread::scope` block to create reference bindings that the scope can capture.\n131\t\n132\tThe `thread::scope` API ensures all spawned threads complete before the scope exits, so all borrows are valid for the thread's lifetime.\n133\t\n134\t### Change 3: Adjust the `current_stream_sync` barrier position\n135\t\n136\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n137\t\n138\tThe existing `current_stream_sync()` at line 1192 ensures prior GPU work is visible to worker threads. Since the background thread does its own GPU uploads and kernel launches on `cudaStreamPerThread`, it has its own implicit stream ordering. The background thread's `current_stream_sync()` at the end ensures its work is complete before the results are used in MLE rounds.\n139\t\n140\tThe existing barrier at line 1192 must remain — it ensures that GPU data uploaded by the main thread (sels, lambda_pows, batch_array, extract tables) is visible to the Round 0 worker threads.\n141\t\n142\t## Invariants\n143\t\n144\t1. **Correctness**: The logup_combinations values are identical — same inputs, same computation, same results. Only the timing changes.\n145\t2. **Stream safety**: The background thread's `cudaStreamPerThread` is independent from the Round 0 worker threads' `cudaStreamPerThread`s. The background thread calls `current_stream_sync()` before returning, ensuring all its GPU work (H2D copies, kernel launches, memory allocations) is complete and visible to all streams.\n146\t3. **No APC 0 regression**: At APC 0, `num_threads = 1` (< 100 AIRs). The background precompute thread still spawns but does minimal work (~5ms for ~99 traces). The single-threaded Round 0 is unaffected.\n147\t4. **Memory pool safety**: The background thread allocates DeviceBuffers through `cudaMallocAsync` on its own stream. These are small allocations (~100 EF elements per trace, total ~600KB). They don't interfere with the Round 0 worker threads' pre-allocated buffers.\n148\t5. **Borrow safety**: All references captured by the background thread are shared borrows (`&`) that coexist with the shared borrows held by Round 0 work items. No mutable aliases exist during the `thread::scope` lifetime.\n149\t\n150\t## Measurement Plan\n151\t\n152\tRun the benchmark in `/home/georg/powdr`:\n153\t```bash\n154\tcd results/pairing\n155\tRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n156\tRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\tAnalyze with `spec.py`:\n160\t```bash\n161\tpython3 ~/spec.py current_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n162\tpython3 ~/spec.py current_apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\n163\t```\n164\t\n165\tExpected results:\n166\t- Round 0 at APC 300: 202ms → ~160ms (20% reduction)\n167\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1327ms → ~1285ms\n168\t- APC 0: no regression (within ±10ms noise)\n169\t\n170\t## Rollback Criteria\n171\t\n172\tRevert if ANY of:\n173\t- Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 25ms (below noise threshold)\n174\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses vs before\n175\t- Any metric at APC 0 regresses by more than 20ms\n176\t- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n177\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8yjQCrAPMh3D8xeAEeUrv","session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"1bc41ced-3208-46ed-bdb3-4af2cf7a394a","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:29:18.534Z"}
