{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RSD2j9U5acrXhuDM9QBeZa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n2\t\n3\tOverlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37ms GPU time) plus ~791 H2D uploads (~5-8ms) run sequentially on the default stream BEFORE Round 0 starts, even though their output is only consumed later during MLE rounds. Round 0 uses only host-side eq_3b values for weight computation, so the device-side precompute is entirely independent. By spawning the precompute on a background thread concurrent with Round 0 (which runs 155ms on 8 streams at ~42% GPU utilization), the ~45ms of precompute work is hidden behind the longer Round 0 phase.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxSMfoMFRfWXeujF85vMgM","session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"5c53a96c-b431-40c8-824d-6673bb49c754","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:35:46.953Z"}
