{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BqrfvyzqkWvqT7XWdTNJ4q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Overlap Logup Combination Precompute with Round 0\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tHide ~22ms per segment of logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b H2D uploads + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) behind the Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running them concurrently on a background thread. The precompute output is only consumed during MLE rounds and has zero data dependencies with Round 0 evaluation. Per-segment Round 0 is 92-93ms; the precompute takes ~22ms per segment. Overlapping saves ~22ms × 2 segments = ~44ms total on STARK excl trace at APC 300.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n10\t\n11\t**Function**: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (line 882)\n12\t\n13\t**Per-segment timing (APC 300)**: ple_round0 = 92-93ms, of which ~22ms is precompute and ~65-70ms is multi-stream evaluation.\n14\t\n15\tCurrent sequential order within this function:\n16\t\n17\t1. **Lines 893-908**: Lambda powers upload + lambda combination precompute (needed for Round 0)\n18\t2. **Lines 912-944**: eq_3b host-side CPU computation (needed for Round 0 weight computation — each work item borrows `&self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx]` at line 1082)\n19\t3. **Lines 945-955**: d_eq_3b device upload — ~395 `to_device()` calls per segment producing `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace`. NOT needed for Round 0. Only used by step 4.\n20\t4. **Lines 957-975**: logup_combinations precompute — iterates over all traces, calls `compute_logup_combinations()` per trace. Each call launches 2 GPU kernels (`precompute_logup_numer_combinations` + `precompute_logup_denom_combinations`). ~791 kernel launches per segment, ~18ms GPU time per segment. NOT needed for Round 0, only for MLE rounds.\n21\t5. **Lines 977-1002**: eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base (needed for Round 0 work items)\n22\t6. **Lines 1014-1137**: Work item construction, sorting, extract tables, batch array\n23\t7. **Line 1192-1194**: `current_stream_sync()` barrier\n24\t8. **Lines 1196+**: Round 0 multi-stream evaluation (~65-70ms, 8 threads at ~42% GPU utilization)\n25\t\n26\tSteps 3-4 total ~22ms per segment and are independent of steps 5-8. There is ample GPU capacity for concurrent precompute kernels during Round 0.\n27\t\n28\t**Data dependency analysis** (verified against source code):\n29\t\n30\t| Data | Used by Round 0? | Used by precompute? | Conflict? |\n31\t|------|-------------------|---------------------|-----------|\n32\t| `self.pk` | Yes (shared &) | Yes (shared &) | No (both read-only) |\n33\t| `self.eq_3b_per_trace` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]` at line 1082) | Yes (read for upload + CPU bus_term_sum) | No (both read-only) |\n34\t| `self.d_eq_3b_per_trace` (device) | No | Yes (written by upload) | No conflict |\n35\t| `self.d_beta_pows` | No (Round 0 uses host-side `beta_pows` via work item field at line 1087) | Yes (read by precompute kernels) | No |\n36\t| `self.logup_combinations` | No (first consumed at line 1739 in MLE rounds) | Yes (written by precompute) | No conflict |\n37\t| `self.beta_pows` (host) | Yes (work items borrow `&[EF]` at line 1087) | Yes (read for bus_term_sum CPU computation in `compute_logup_combinations` line 570) | No (both read-only) |\n38\t\n39\t## Changes\n40\t\n41\t### Change 1: Restructure `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` to overlap precompute with Round 0\n42\t\n43\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n44\t\n45\t**What**: Reorder the function body so that steps 3-4 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) run on a background thread concurrent with step 8 (Round 0 multi-stream evaluation). Only applied in the multi-threaded path (num_threads > 1); the single-threaded path retains the current sequential behavior.\n46\t\n47\t**New flow**:\n48\t\n49\t```\n50\t1. Lambda powers + lambda combinations            (sequential, same as before)\n51\t2. eq_3b CPU computation → self.eq_3b_per_trace    (sequential, same as before)\n52\t3. eq_xis + sels_per_trace_base                    (sequential, MOVED BEFORE precompute)\n53\t4. Work item construction + sorting + extract tables + batch array  (sequential)\n54\t5. current_stream_sync() barrier\n55\t6. IF num_threads > 1:\n56\t     std::thread::scope:\n57\t       ├─ Background thread: d_eq_3b upload + logup_combinations precompute\n58\t       │   → returns (Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>>, Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>>)\n59\t       │   → calls current_stream_sync() before returning\n60\t       └─ Round 0 worker threads (0..num_threads): process_air_round0 (same as before)\n61\t     Store background thread results into self\n62\t   ELSE (num_threads <= 1):\n63\t     d_eq_3b upload + logup_combinations precompute (sequential, same as current code)\n64\t     Single-threaded Round 0 evaluation\n65\t7. Continue to MLE rounds (which consume self.logup_combinations)\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t**Specific code changes**:\n69\t\n70\ta) **Move lines 977-1002 (eq_xis + sels) to before lines 945** — these currently sit between the precompute and work item construction but are independent of the precompute. Moving them earlier doesn't change behavior.\n71\t\n72\tb) **Remove lines 945-975 (d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute) from their current position.** They will be placed inside the `thread::scope` block for the multi-threaded path and kept sequential for the single-threaded path.\n73\t\n74\tc) **In the multi-threaded path** (the existing `thread::scope` block that spawns Round 0 worker threads, around line 1292), spawn one additional background thread before the Round 0 workers:\n75\t\n76\t```rust\n77\t// Capture shared references for the background thread\n78\tlet pk_ref = self.pk;\n79\tlet eq_3b_ref = &self.eq_3b_per_trace;\n80\tlet d_beta_pows_ref = &self.d_beta_pows;\n81\tlet beta_pows_ref = &self.beta_pows;\n82\tlet per_trace_ref = &ctx.per_trace;\n83\t\n84\tstd::thread::scope(|s| {\n85\t    // Background thread: upload d_eq_3b + precompute logup combinations\n86\t    let precompute_handle = s.spawn(|| -> Result<_, LogupZerocheckError> {\n87\t        let d_eq_3b: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = eq_3b_ref\n88\t            .iter()\n89\t            .map(|eq_3bs| {\n90\t                if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n91\t                    Ok(DeviceBuffer::new())\n92\t                } else {\n93\t                    eq_3bs.to_device().map_err(MemCopyError::from)\n94\t                }\n95\t            })\n96\t            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n97\t\n98\t        let mut logup_combs: Vec<Option<LogupCombinations>> =\n99\t            (0..num_present_airs).map(|_| None).collect();\n100\t        for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in per_trace_ref.iter().enumerate() {\n101\t            let air_pk = &pk_ref.per_air[*air_idx];\n102\t            if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some()\n103\t                && !eq_3b_ref[trace_idx].is_empty()\n104\t            {\n105\t                logup_combs[trace_idx] = Some(\n106\t                    compute_logup_combinations(\n107\t                        pk_ref, *air_idx, d_beta_pows_ref,\n108\t                        &d_eq_3b[trace_idx], &eq_3b_ref[trace_idx], beta_pows_ref,\n109\t                    ).map_err(LogupZerocheckError::LogupCombinations)?\n110\t                );\n111\t            }\n112\t        }\n113\t\n114\t        // Ensure all GPU work on this thread's stream is visible\n115\t        current_stream_sync().map_err(MemCopyError::from)?;\n116\t        Ok((d_eq_3b, logup_combs))\n117\t    });\n118\t\n119\t    // Spawn Round 0 worker threads (same as current code)\n120\t    let round0_handles: Vec<_> = (0..num_threads).map(|tid| {\n121\t        s.spawn(move || { /* existing process_air_round0 logic */ })\n122\t    }).collect();\n123\t\n124\t    // Join all\n125\t    // ... collect round0 results ...\n126\t    let precompute_result = precompute_handle.join().unwrap()?;\n127\t    (round0_results, precompute_result)\n128\t});\n129\t\n130\t// Store precompute results\n131\tself.d_eq_3b_per_trace = precompute_result.0;\n132\tself.logup_combinations = precompute_result.1;\n133\t```\n134\t\n135\td) **In the single-threaded path** (num_threads <= 1, around line 1272): keep the d_eq_3b upload + logup precompute in sequential order, same as current code. The overlap provides no benefit here since the single-threaded Round 0 already saturates the GPU for the few large AIRs.\n136\t\n137\t### Change 2: Handle borrow references for the background thread\n138\t\n139\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n140\t\n141\tBefore the `thread::scope` block, create local reference bindings that the scope can capture:\n142\t```rust\n143\tlet pk_ref = self.pk;\n144\tlet eq_3b_ref = &self.eq_3b_per_trace;\n145\tlet d_beta_pows_ref = &self.d_beta_pows;\n146\tlet beta_pows_ref = &self.beta_pows;\n147\tlet per_trace_ref = &ctx.per_trace;\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\tThese are all shared borrows (`&`) that coexist with the shared borrows already taken by Round 0 work items. `thread::scope` ensures all threads complete before the scope exits, so all borrows are valid.\n151\t\n152\t### Change 3: Ensure correct stream synchronization\n153\t\n154\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n155\t\n156\tThree synchronization points are needed:\n157\t\n158\t1. **Existing barrier (line 1192)**: `current_stream_sync()` — ensures main-thread GPU uploads (sels, lambda_pows, batch_array, extract tables) are visible to Round 0 worker threads. Stays as-is.\n159\t\n160\t2. **Background thread exit**: `current_stream_sync()` inside the background thread ensures all d_eq_3b uploads and precompute kernel launches are complete before the thread returns results. This is critical because the `LogupCombinations` contain `DeviceBuffer` objects allocated on the background thread's `cudaStreamPerThread`. Without this sync, the buffers might not be visible to other streams.\n161\t\n162\t3. **No additional barrier needed after thread::scope**: Rust's `thread::scope` guarantees the background thread has completed (including its `current_stream_sync()`) before the scope returns. The returned `DeviceBuffer` objects are ready for use on any stream.\n163\t\n164\t## Invariants\n165\t\n166\t1. **Correctness**: The logup_combinations values are identical — same inputs, same computation, same results. Only the timing changes.\n167\t2. **Stream safety**: Background thread's `cudaStreamPerThread` is independent from Round 0 worker threads' streams. The background thread's `current_stream_sync()` at exit ensures all GPU work is globally visible.\n168\t3. **No APC 0 regression**: At APC 0, num_threads = 1 (< 100 AIRs). The single-threaded path is unchanged — no background thread is spawned.\n169\t4. **Memory pool interaction**: The background thread allocates DeviceBuffers through `cudaMallocAsync` on its own stream. These are small allocations (~800 bytes per trace, ~600KB total). Round 0 workers use pre-allocated buffers for 95% of AIRs (from the threshold prealloc optimization), so mutex contention between the background thread and Round 0 workers is minimal (~30 fallback allocations from Round 0 vs ~791 precompute allocations — the mutex acquisition cost of ~2us × 800 = ~1.6ms is negligible).\n170\t5. **Borrow safety**: All references captured by the background thread are shared borrows (`&`) that coexist with the shared borrows held by Round 0 work items. No mutable aliases exist during the `thread::scope` lifetime. The background thread returns owned values, which are stored into `self` only after the scope exits.\n171\t\n172\t## Measurement Plan\n173\t\n174\tRun the benchmark in `/home/georg/powdr`:\n175\t```bash\n176\tcd results/pairing\n177\tRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n178\tRUST_LOG=info powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics current_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n179\t```\n180\t\n181\tAnalyze with `spec.py`:\n182\t```bash\n183\tpython3 ~/spec.py current_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n184\tpython3 ~/spec.py current_apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\n185\t```\n186\t\n187\tCheck per-segment breakdown:\n188\t```python\n189\t# Verify per-segment ple_round0_time_ms decreased by ~20ms each\n190\tpython3 -c \"import json; [print(g) for g in json.load(open('metrics.json'))['gauge'] if 'ple_round0' in g['metric']]\"\n191\t```\n192\t\n193\tExpected results:\n194\t- ple_round0 per segment at APC 300: 92-93ms → ~70-73ms (~22ms reduction each)\n195\t- Round 0 total at APC 300: 202ms → ~158ms\n196\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1327ms → ~1285ms\n197\t- APC 0: no regression (unchanged single-threaded path)\n198\t\n199\t## Rollback Criteria\n200\t\n201\tRevert if ANY of:\n202\t- Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 25ms total (below noise threshold for 2-segment sum)\n203\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses vs before\n204\t- Any metric at APC 0 regresses by more than 20ms\n205\t- Correctness failure (proof verification fails)\n206\t- LogUp GKR or other phases regress by more than 15ms at APC 300 (indicating memory pool disruption from concurrent allocations)\n207\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxSMfoMFRfWXeujF85vMgM","session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"6c2b36b7-ac99-4c4d-bc05-a8148bb79a30","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:35:47.637Z"}
