{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3DpJNcijazJffExbUo7Zy","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n\nOverlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37ms GPU time) plus ~791 H2D uploads (~5-8ms) run sequentially on the default stream BEFORE Round 0 starts, even though their output is only consumed later during MLE rounds. Round 0 uses only host-side eq_3b values for weight computation, so the device-side precompute is entirely independent. By spawning the precompute on a background thread concurrent with Round 0 (which runs 155ms on 8 streams at ~42% GPU utilization), the ~45ms of precompute work is hidden behind the longer Round 0 phase.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n206 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current metrics exist ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 1050639 Apr 14 07:39 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 2092799 Apr 14 07:39 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff03fa2a-06a9-4cae-9336-eb9eb1af38e2","uuid":"c54afd0b-53d2-476d-8ab8-a61ccdde4448","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:39:56.518Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n\nOverlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37